<title>SPAIN: BNP to take Spanish unit off bourse.</title>
<headline>BNP to take Spanish unit off bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Nationale de Paris has asked to remove its Spanish unit from the bourse ahead of a proposed capital reduction, Spain's stock market commission said on Monday.</p>
<p>The commission later said it was suspending trade in BNP Espana on all Spanish bourses effective on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The parent bank, BNP, which owns 97.4 percent of the share capital of its affiliate, will ask shareholders on June 27 to approve a capital reduction of 583 million pesetas that would take two pesetas off the nominal share price shrinking it from 75 pesetas to 73 pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
